<title>EGYPT: Impounded Ukrainian ship escapes from Egypt port.</title>
<headline>Impounded Ukrainian ship escapes from Egypt port.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Ukrainian ship impounded in the Red Sea port of Suez has slipped out of Egyptian territorial waters without paying outstanding dues, shipping sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The Musa-Dzhalil was impounded by port authorities on Sunday after a court ordered its owner Black Sea Shipping Co. (BLASCO) to pay its agent in Egypt $180,000, the sources said.</p>
<p>&quot;Later, the agent found that the ship disappeared from the port,&quot; one source told Reuters.</p>
<p>The ship was carrying 11,953 tonnes of fertilisers from Ukraine to Malaysia.</p>
</text>
